  "6df90fcb-e72b-4614-aa1c-52f7b54ab1d1": {
   "id": "6df90fcb-e72b-4614-aa1c-52f7b54ab1d1",
   "message": {
    "id": "6df90fcb-e72b-4614-aa1c-52f7b54ab1d1",
    "author": {
     "role": "assistant",
     "name": null,
     "metadata": {}
    },
    "create_time": 1764729482.424,
    "update_time": null,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "Export the run (or use the lap data) and split it in half by time:\n\n1. First half: average pace (or speed) and average HR → ratio₁ = speed₁ / HR₁\n2. Second half: ratio₂ = speed₂ / HR₂\n3. Decoupling % = (ratio₁ − ratio₂) / ratio₁ × 100\n\nExample: 1st half 9:00/mi at 140 bpm, 2nd half 9:00/mi at 148 bpm → speed is equal, so decoupling = (1/140 − 1/148)/(1/140) = 5.4%.\n\nIgnore the first ~10 minutes of warm-up if HR is still settling. In a sheet, `=(A2/B2 - A3/B3)/(A2/B2)` with speed in A and HR in B."
     ]
    },
